<article class="env-lemma" id="08D9">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/08D9">Lemma <span data-tag="08D9">36.7.3</span>.</a> Let $X = \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(A)$ be an affine scheme. Then </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$Q_ X : \textit{Mod}(\mathcal{O}_ X) \to \mathit{QCoh}(\mathcal{O}_ X)$ is the functor which sends $\mathcal{F}$ to the quasi-coherent $\mathcal{O}_ X$-module associated to the $A$-module $\Gamma (X, \mathcal{F})$, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$RQ_ X : D(\mathcal{O}_ X) \to D(\mathit{QCoh}(\mathcal{O}_ X))$ is the functor which sends $E$ to the complex of quasi-coherent $\mathcal{O}_ X$-modules associated to the object $R\Gamma (X, E)$ of $D(A)$, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
restricted to $D_\mathit{QCoh}(\mathcal{O}_ X)$ the functor $RQ_ X$ defines a quasi-inverse to (<a href="/tag/06VT" data-tag="06VT">36.3.0.1</a>). 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      The functor $Q_ X$ is the functor 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  \mathcal{F} \mapsto \widetilde{\Gamma (X, \mathcal{F})}  \]
</div>
    <p>
       by Schemes, Lemma <a href="/tag/01I7" data-tag="01I7">26.7.1</a>. This immediately implies (1) and (2). The third assertion follows from (the proof of) Lemma <a href="/tag/06Z0" data-tag="06Z0">36.3.5</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>